"help" = "🌰 Usage:\n  kastan route|from to\n  kastan station\n  kastan suggest <text> [-T alias] [-o text|markdown|html|json] [-l count]\n  kastan stations <name> [-T alias] [-o text|markdown|html|json] [-l count]\n  kastan connections route|from to|-f place -t place [-V place] [-T alias] [-d d.m.yyyy] [-m h:mm] [-a|-p] [-x] [-X count] [-M minutes] [-c] [-v] [-o text|markdown|html|json|ics] [-l count]\n  kastan departures station|-f place|-s place [-T alias] [-d d.m.yyyy] [-m h:mm] [-a|-p] [-v] [-o text|markdown|html|json] [-l count]\n  kastan station-timetables -L line -f stop -t direction [-T alias] [-u municipality] [-d d.m.yyyy] [-w] [-o text|markdown|html|json]\n  kastan service <service-id> [-T alias] [-o text|markdown|html|json]\n  kastan aliases list|add|remove|path [-o text|markdown|html|json]\n  kastan timetables [-o text|markdown|html|json]\n\n⚙️ Options:\n  -h, --help              Show help\n  --version               Show the app version\n  --language, --lang      Output language: en or cs (defaults to the system language)\n  --source                {0}\n  -f, --from              Departure place or station\n  -t, --to                Arrival place or direction stop\n  -s, --station           Station for departures or arrivals\n  -L, --line              MHD line for Station Timetables\n  -T, --timetable         Timetable identifier supplied by the selected data source\n  -u, --municipality      Integrated-system municipality for Station Timetables\n  -d, --date              Search date\n  -m, --time              Search time\n  -w, --whole-week        Show Station Timetables for the whole week\n  -a, --arrival           Search by arrival time instead of departure time\n  -p, --departure         Search by departure time\n  -V, --via               Via place, repeat for multiple places\n  -x, --direct            Direct connections only\n  -c, --add-to-calendar   Open the first returned connection as an iCalendar import\n  -v, --verbose           Show result and service IDs, tariff zones, platforms, carriers, and delay details\n  -X, --max-transfers     Maximum transfers permitted, including 0\n  -M, --min-transfer-time Minimum transfer time in minutes, including 0\n  -o, --format            Output format: text, markdown, html, json, or ics for connections\n  -l, --limit             Maximum number of printed results\n\n{1}Stop aliases are stored in ~/.config/kastan/aliases.json unless KASTAN_ALIAS_DATABASE is set.";
